Classic camera public-driver JPEG fixture
=========================================

Files in this directory: shared bootloader/bootloader.bin,
shared partition_table/partition-table.bin, jpeg.bin, jpeg-psram.bin and the
host inputs jpeg/qvga-a.jpg, jpeg/qvga-b.jpg, jpeg/vga-a.jpg, jpeg/vga-b.jpg,
and jpeg/browser-420.jpg.
Source and pinned rebuild recipe: examples/classic-camera/jpeg.md.

Linked application code is the simulator-owned MIT fixture, ESP-IDF v5.4.3
and esp32-camera b817e9b81041980608d1a3d3e0b08d86e3666382 (Apache-2.0),
Mbed TLS SHA-256 (Apache-2.0), FreeRTOS (MIT), TLSF (BSD-3-Clause),
Xtensa HAL (MIT), newlib (per-file licences), and GCC runtime
(GPLv3 with GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1). jpeg-psram.bin additionally
links the ESP-IDF esp_psram component (Apache-2.0).
The bootloader contains the same applicable ESP-IDF/runtime components.

Full third-party licence texts are at the repository-root path
web/wasm/fw/public/classic-hello-NOTICE.txt (ESP-IDF, Mbed TLS, FreeRTOS, newlib, GCC runtime,
TLSF and Xtensa HAL). The MIT application licence is the repository LICENSE.
The Apache-2.0 text there also applies to esp32-camera, Copyright Espressif
Systems (Shanghai) CO LTD. esp32-camera source is unchanged.

Inventory checked from the application link maps. esp_jpeg 1.3.1 is a pinned
build dependency, but no JPEG encoder or decoder is linked into these images:
the guest receives already-encoded bytes and only hashes them. The four .jpg
files are generated by examples/classic-camera/make-jpeg.py (MIT, standard
library only); they contain no third-party data. browser-420.jpg is a self-made
2x2 RGB image encoded with libjpeg-turbo cjpeg 3.2.0 (-baseline -sample 2x2
-quality 75); its input and hash are documented in docs/evidence/classic-cam-jpeg/README.md.
No ROM ELF is redistributed here; tools/fetch-rom-elfs.sh fetches it separately.
